.TH DASHBOARD 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dashboard \- Static single-page home PV monitoring dashboard with a
Prometheus proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dashboard
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Static single-page home PV monitoring dashboard (energy flow diagram,
energy summary and chart) fed by Prometheus through the bundled
stdlib-only proxy: the browser loads the static app from the server, the
app's queries go to \fB/prom\fR and are proxied to the upstream
Prometheus (\fB--upstream\fR). The front-end configuration is served as
/config.js (the SOLAR_CONFIG object; \fB--battery\fR injects the battery
panels).
.PP
The HTTP surface is the tool's serving surface: the connection caps
(\fB--max-clients\fR total, \fB--max-conn-per-ip\fR per peer, extras
get an immediate 503), the idle keep-alive kick (\fB--client-timeout\fR).
The README documents the loopback/reverse-proxy paths \(em the server
speaks plain HTTP with no authentication on page or proxy yet (the auth
story in docs/TODO.md): bind the loopback or put a proxy in front.
.PP
The JSON-lines control server (\fB--control-port\fR, talked to with
\fBdashboard-ctl\fR(1) and \fBdashboard-cli\fR(1)) inspects and steers
the running server: the live settings (the caps, the log surface, the
battery flag), the config reload, the graceful shutdown. With a control
token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: every command and reply carries
the full sha256 of its payload, keyed by the token (common/wiresec.py)
\(em a token-holding client verifies both directions, and over TCP the
signed commands are mandatory. A second, read-only token
(\fB--control-ops-token\fR) authenticates into the show/clear verbs only
\(em the ops shift against the admin key, both roles audited.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
listen port (default: config file, $PORT or 8080)
.TP
.B \-\-bind
address to bind (default: config file, $BIND or 0.0.0.0)
.TP
.B \-\-upstream
upstream Prometheus URL (default: config file, $PROM_URL or
http://localhost:9090)
.TP
.B \-\-prom\-prefix
path under which Prometheus is proxied (default: config file,
$PROM_PREFIX or /prom); empty string proxies everything
.TP
.B \-\-static\-dir
directory to serve (default: config file, $STATIC_DIR or static next to
the script)
.TP
.B \-\-config\-js
config.js to serve at /config.js (default: config file, $CONFIG_JS or
config.js next to the script)
.TP
.B \-\-battery
enable battery support in the served config.js (default: config file,
$BATTERY or off)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-clients " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP clients (pages + proxy); extras get an immediate
503 (default: config file, $MAX_CLIENTS or 64; 0 = unlimited)
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-timeout " N"
seconds an idle keep\-alive HTTP client is kept before being kicked
(default: config file, $CLIENT_TIMEOUT or 300; 0 = off)
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-conn\-per\-ip " N"
maximum concurrent HTTP connections from one peer IP; extras get an
immediate 503 (default: config file, $MAX_CONN_PER_IP or 0 = no per\-IP
limit)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
JSON\-lines control server target: unix socket path (default:
/tmp/dashboard\-<port>.socket) or TCP port number on 127.0.0.1 (e.g.
15598); 0 = off. Talk to it with dashboard\-ctl.py (default: config
file, $CTL)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
require a token on control connections: the client authenticates with
{"cmd": "auth", "token": ...}; over the unix socket a trusted peer
(root, the daemon's own user or \-\-control\-trust\-uids — SO_PEERCRED)
skips the token; the value may be `file:<path>` — the first line of an
owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential rides as
file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config file, $CONTROL_TOKEN or
none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token\-file
the control token from a file (the first line; e.g. a systemd
LoadCredential or a key file; must be owner\-only 0600) — takes the
place of \-\-control\-token; giving both is an error (env
CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-ops\-token
a second, read\-only control token: sessions authenticating with it may
run the show/clear verbs only (no set/unset, no request reload, no
shutdown) — the ops shift against the admin key, both audited; the value
may be `file:<path>` — the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a
systemd LoadCredential rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default:
config file, $CONTROL_OPS_TOKEN or none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-ops\-token\-file
the read\-only ops token from a file (the first line; must be
owner\-only 0600) — takes the place of \-\-control\-ops\-token; giving
both is an error (env CONTROL_OPS_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-trust\-uids
extra peer uids the unix control socket trusts without the token
(SO_PEERCRED — a local systemd unit speaks without the secret); root and
the daemon's own user are always trusted (default: config file,
$CONTROL_TRUST_UIDS or none)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-ops\-verbs
the read\-only ops role's RBAC policy: the verbs its sessions may run,
comma\-separated (default: show,clear; validated against the control
grammar at start)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-server
serve the dashboard's own Prometheus /metrics endpoint (the uptime, the
request counters, the proxied query total, the client gate) — off by
default and a token is mandatory when on (default: config file,
$METRICS_SERVER or off)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-listen
the metrics bind address HOST:PORT (default: config file,
$METRICS_LISTEN or 127.0.0.1:9452)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-token
require Authorization: Bearer <token> on the /metrics endpoint —
mandatory when \-\-metrics\-server is on; the value may be `file:<path>`
— the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential
rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config file,
$METRICS_TOKEN)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-token\-file
the metrics bearer token from a file (the first line; must be
owner\-only 0600) — takes the place of \-\-metrics\-token; giving both
is an error (env METRICS_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-max\-clients " N"
maximum concurrent /metrics clients; extras get an immediate 503, 0 =
unlimited (default: config file, $METRICS_MAX_CLIENTS or 16)
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-client\-timeout " N"
seconds an idle /metrics client is kept before the socket times out, 0 =
the built\-in 5 s cap (default: config file, $METRICS_CLIENT_TIMEOUT or
5)
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-max\-conn\-per\-ip " N"
maximum concurrent /metrics connections from one peer IP, 0 = no per\-IP
limit (default: config file, $METRICS_MAX_CONN_PER_IP or 0)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
DSH audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout (the docker/journald way);
default: the XDG state home (~/.local/state/dashboard/audit.log)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size in MB, keeping 3 backups; 0 = no size
rotation (default 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the DSH audit trail (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level
log level (default: config file or INFO); DEBUG logs every request
.TP
.B \-\-log\-queries
log proxied Prometheus queries at INFO level
.TP
.B \-\-log\-access
log every HTTP request at INFO (default: config file, $LOG_ACCESS or
quiet)
.TP
.B \-\-local\-time
log timestamps in the system time zone instead of UTC (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-path
the state dump: the live setting overrides (the toggles, the caps, the
log surface — the tokens apart) as one JSON, written 0600 with an
integrity hash (a restore refuses a tampered, unsigned or
group\-writable dump); dumped on the request dump command and the
graceful shutdown; loaded on start only with \-\-restore\-on\-start, on
demand with the request restore command (default: config file,
$DUMP_PATH or none)
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-key
the key that seals the state dumps and the reload's state file: the
state rides encrypted (an HMAC\-SHA256 counter\-mode keystream,
authenticated — a restore refuses a wrong or missing key, and a
configured key refuses an unsealed dump); the reload re\-exec
re\-resolves the same key, so the state file reads on the other side; no
key = the dumps stay 0600 plaintext with the integrity hash; a dump path
without a key warns at start and on set; the value may be `file:<path>`
— the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file (a systemd LoadCredential
rides as file:/run/credentials/...) (default: config file, $DUMP_KEY or
none)
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-on\-start
load the state dump when the server starts (needs \-\-dump\-path) — the
live overrides ride again instead of a cold start; default: start cold,
load only on demand (default: config file, $RESTORE_ON_START) (default:
off)
.TP
.B \-\-config
config file — the set grammar: every line a `set <name> <value>`,
comments start with # (default: $CONFIG, then server.conf next to this
script, then the subproject root) (default:
/Users/oom/GensparkCode/pv\-dash/dashboard/server.conf)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
validate the configuration, print the effective settings and exit
(nothing is bound) (default: off)


.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
re-read the config file and apply what is live (the same path as the
control server's request reload); the listen address and port are bound
and stay.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
graceful shutdown (the connected consoles get the daemon-exit frame).

.SH CONTROL
The control server speaks JSON lines ({"cmd": "..."} ->
{"status": "ok|err|bye", "text": "..."}; TCP requires the token when
configured and refuses to start without one). Commands:
\fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/\fBhelp\fR (the settings: max-clients,
client-timeout, max-conn-per-ip, log-access, log-queries, battery,
log-level \(em and the token lives: control token, the ops token,
metrics token, each rotating live, the value never rendering \(em
\fBshow <secret>\fR refuses), \fBshow status\fR, \fBshow connections\fR
(the live HTTP clients), \fBshow version\fR, \fBshow knobs\fR
(the dictionary of the registry), \fBinspect\fR,
\fBrequest reload\fR (the SIGHUP path), \fBreload\fR (the
whole-daemon restart that keeps the sets: the live overrides save to a
state file beside the config, the process re-execs, the fresh daemon
re-applies them once), with a dump path configured (\fB--dump-path\fR):
\fBrequest dump\fR / \fBrequest restore\fR (the overrides as one 0600
integrity-hashed JSON; \fB--dump-key\fR seals it \(em the state rides
encrypted, a restore refuses a wrong or missing key;
\fB--restore-on-start\fR loads it at start),
\fBshutdown\fR, \fBquit\fR. See
.BR dashboard-ctl (1)
and
.BR dashboard-cli (1).

.SH SECURITY
The server speaks plain HTTP and has no authentication on the page or the
proxy yet (the auth story in docs/TODO.md): bind the loopback (the NixOS
module's default) or publish the port loopback-only and put an
authenticating reverse proxy in front for anything beyond localhost. The
control surface is loopback-only (TCP) or a 0600 unix socket; a TCP
control port without a token refuses to start (F5); with a token the wire
is signed and the commands/replies verify end to end; a second, read-only
ops token (\fB--control-ops-token\fR) scopes its sessions to the
show/clear verbs. The audit trail (default in the XDG state home, prefix
DSH) records the control commands with their roles, the auth failures, the
reloads and the shutdowns.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/dashboard-<port>.socket
the default control socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dashboard/audit.log
the default audit trail.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dashboard-ctl (1),
.BR dashboard-cli (1),
.BR modbus-scraper (1),
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1)
.PP
dashboard/README.md in the suite checkout \(em the full documentation.
